# Chapter 7. Adding the Stochastic Hill-Climber Learning Algorithm

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:nx, "1.0.0"},
  {:kino, "0.19.1"},
  {:kino_vega_lite, "0.1.13"}
])
```

## Reader's guide

**Neuroevolution through Elixir**  
Part II - Neuroevolution: Taking the First Step

**The central idea:** keep the best weights, propose a perturbation, evaluate it,
and either accept it or restore the previous weights. When a run stops improving,
start again without losing the best network found across runs.

This notebook remasters Gene I. Sher's *Handbook of Neuroevolution Through Erlang*
(2013), Chapter 7, printed pp. 187-227, referred to as **[S]**. It retains Sections
**7.1-7.9**, including **7.1.1** and **7.6.1-7.6.9**. Page references below are
printed page numbers, not PDF indices.

Sher supplies the augmented stochastic hill climber, trainer, exoself,
private/public scape distinction, XOR interface, and repeated-run benchmark.
**All Elixir/Nx code, the three-way architecture comparison, recorded random tapes,
new diagrams, and executable checks are remaster implementations.** Corrections
and engineering choices are identified rather than silently attributed to Sher.

### Three implementations, one optimization contract

| Stage | Implementation | What remains explicit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Thesis | Scalar Elixir actors: sensor, neurons, actuator, cortex, scape; trainer and exoself tasks | Messages, episode boundaries, weight backup and restoration |
| Antithesis | Actor-free Nx numerical core, including the complete random-restart search loop | Tensor state, masks, acceptance, patience, archive, termination |
| Synthesis | Trainer/exoself actors controlling a network-level Nx actor | Coarse process ownership with tensor inference and mutation |

The synthesis is **not** another process around every tensor scalar. One worker
owns the complete network's tensor parameters. All three versions use the same
parameter order, recorded random draws, scoring rule, and stopping policy.

### Chapter map

| Section | Question | Main artifact |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 7.1 | How does augmented hill climbing work? | Two patience counters and a perturbation law |
